TestNG ---> Test Next Generation.
--> TestNG is a testing framework inspired from JUnit and NUnit but introducing some new functionalities that make it more powerful and easier to use.
--> Helps us:
    1. Organize testcases
    2. Execute tests in sequences
    3. Execute tests in parallel
    4. Group testcases
    5. Generate test reports
    6. manage testdata
    7. Run selected testcases using testng.xml.

testng.xml ---> configuration file used to control the execution of testng testcases
  It tells testng:
    1. Which testcases to run
    2. In which order to run them
    3. How many times to run them
    4. Which groups of testcases to run
    5. Which parameters to pass to the test (browser, env, url, user credentials ,etcc....)

dependsonMethod  -->
     1. previous test should be executed before the current test case
     2. If previous test case fails, current test case will be skipped

alwaysRun  -->
     1. If previous test case fails, current test case will be executed
     2. no direct dependency